findings.proposed_change:
Add one private lemma, stated once for an arbitrary source Y and independent of which `ofInjectiveResolution` supplies the short complex:

private lemma subsingleton_ext_cyclesShortComplex_X₂ (X Y : C) (I : InjectiveResolution A) (n q : ℕ) (hq : 0 < q) : Subsingleton (Ext Y ((AcyclicResolution.ofInjectiveResolution X I).cyclesShortComplex n).X₂ q)

Proof sketch: `change Subsingleton (Ext Y (I.cocomplex.X n) q)`, then `exact (AcyclicResolution.ofInjectiveResolution Y I).extAcyclic n q hq`. Alternatively, obtain q = q'+1 and use `subsingleton_of_injective`, as in `AcyclicResolution.ofInjectiveResolution`. Each use site then becomes one line, e.g. `haveI := subsingleton_ext_cyclesShortComplex_X₂ X X I n q hq`, or four lines `haveI := lemma X Y I n (q+1) (by omega)` for the Y and q variants. The same lemma replaces the blocks in `injectiveCyclesCokernelIso`, the `_inv_source_naturality_apply` lemma and `injectiveExtPositiveIsoHomology_source_naturality`, using `q := 1` and `n := q - 1` where needed. It can also be an `instance` for q = 1.

